          %h2#idea_and_definition Idea and definition
          %p
            The notion of
            %em Kähler differential
            is a very general way to encode a notion of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+field"} vector field
          %p
            Conceptually, in dual language of algebras, a symmetry of a commutative algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism"} automorphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\colon A\to A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(a b)=g(a)g(b)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivations"} derivations
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\colon A\to A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi b
                    %mo +
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X(a b)=X(a)b+X(b)a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            of Kähler differentials
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi K
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1_K(A)
            parametrizes derivations, in the sense that every derivation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            corresponds uniquely to a morphism of
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi K
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_X: \Omega_K^1 (A)\to A
          %h3#the_ordinary_definition_and_its_insufficiency The ordinary definition and its insufficiency
          %p
            Kähler differentials are traditionally conceived in terms of an algebraic construction of a certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi K
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_K^1(Spec R)
            on a given ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CRing"} CRing
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ^{op}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/varieties"} varieties
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+space"} algebraic space
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne-Mumford+stack"} Deligne-Mumford stack
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
            in this context. This is the case discussed in the section
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#OrdinaryRings"} Over ordinary rings
          %p below.
          %p
            The definition, concrete as it is, applies of course also to function rings on spaces not modeled on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi CRing
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing^{op}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)
            of smooth functions on a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spec
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_K(Spec C^\infty(X))
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#SmoothOrPlain"}> Over smooth rings regarded as ordinary rings
              \.
          %p
            This shows that the concrete algebraic construction of Kähler differential forms over plain rings, traditionally thought of as their very definition, does in fact not correctly capture their nature. There is another definition – obtained from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nPOV"} nPOV
            – which does capture the situation correctly:
          %h3#the_correct_definition_of_the_notion_of_module_
            The correct definition of the notion of
            %em module
            …
          %p
            In fact, already the definition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            has to be freed from it concrete realization in the context of ordinary rings, to exhibit its true nature. What this is has been established long ago in
          %ul
            %li
              Dan Quillen,
              %em Homotopical algebra
          %p
            and in Jon Beck’s thesis, and is discussed in more detail in the entries
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            and
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beck+module"} Beck module
            \: Beck and Quillen noticed that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R Mod
            of modules over an ordinary commutative ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is canonically
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
            to the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi CRing
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab(CRing/R)
            of abelian
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CRing
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing/R
            of all rings, over the given ring
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Ab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi CRing
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  R Mod \simeq Ab(CRing/R)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Under this equivalence an
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            is sent to the square-0-extension ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \oplus N
            that is canonically equipped with a ring homomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi N
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \oplus N \to R
            and with a unital and associative and commutative product operation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (R \oplus N) \times_R (R \oplus N) \to (R \oplus N)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi r
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi n
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi r
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi n
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi r
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi n
                    %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi n
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  ((r, n_1), (r,n_2)) \mapsto (r, n_1 + n_2)
          %p
            that makes it first an object in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CRing
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing/R
            and in there an abelian group object, hence an object in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi CRing
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab(CRing/R)
          %p
            Conversely, every module arises this way, up to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          %p
            And this is the right definition. Notably, this definition does not assume anything about the ring
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is a ring at all! It could be anything.
          %p
            Concretely: for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %em any
            category of test objects – so that we may think of objects in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op}
            as function rings on the test objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            – we may define the category of
            %em module
            s over an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \in C^{op}
            by the above equation:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi Ab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  R Mod := Ab(C^{op}/R)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Notice that this is now a definition. And that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            could be anything, and the definition still makes sense.
          %p
            The category of all modules over
            %em all
            possible objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is then nothing but the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain+fibration"} codomain fibration
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Mod
                    %mi C
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi Ab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi I
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mi C
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Mod_C := Ab([I,C^{op}]) \stackrel{p_C}{\to} C^{op}
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+category"} interval category
            and fiberwise (over
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op}
          %p
            This turns out to be the correct
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theoretic
            definition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            (as discussed there). In fact, this is is the special case of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher categorical
            definition that works for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            any
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab(C^{op}/R)
            of abelian group objects in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategory
            is generalized (straightforwardly! and in fact even more elegantly) to the notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} tangent (∞,1)-category
          %h3#AbstractDef
            … and the correct definition of
            %em derivations
            and
            %em Kähler modules
          %p
            With the above correct notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            in hand, all the other concepts of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+theory"} deformation theory
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                given an
                = succeed "-module" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
                regarded as an object
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mi N
                        %mo :
                        %mi R
                        %mo ⊕
                        %mi N
                        %mo →
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_N : R \oplus N \to R
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"}> derivation
                  s
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                with coefficients in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
                are precisely the
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi δ
                      %mo :
                      %mi R
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta : R \to R \oplus N
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_N
            %li
              %p
                The assignment
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spec
                      %mi R
                      %mo ↦
                      %msub
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Spec
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec R \mapsto \Omega_K(Spec R)
                of modules of
                = succeed "s" do
                  %strong Kähler differential
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi K
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi Mod
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\Omega_K : C^{op} \to Mod_C
              %p
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
                to the above projection
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mi C
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mi Mod
                          %mi C
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_C : Mod_C \to C^{op}
              %p
                this means that every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi δ
                      %mo :
                      %mi R
                      %mo →
                      %mi 𝒩
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta : R \to \mathcal{N}
                (being a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                of the module which is the overcategory element
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒩
                        %mo →
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N} \to R
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi 𝒩
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_K(R) \to \mathcal{N}
                in the category of abelian
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategory
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op}/R
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Mod
                            %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝒩
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mi op
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝒩
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      Hom_{Mod_C}(\Omega_K(R), \mathcal{N})
                      \\simeq
                      Hom_{C^{op}}(R, \mathcal{N})
                      \\,.
          %p
            Notice that in all of the above now,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is still a completely arbitrary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
          %h3#the_fully_general_definition The fully general definition
          %p
            By allowing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            – the collection of test spaces – to be a general
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nPOV"} nPOV
            on the nature of Kähler differentials:
          .standout
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              of test spaces, write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                    %mo :
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_{C^{op}} : Mod := T_{C^{op}} \to C^{op}
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} tangent (∞,1)-category
              of its
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the fiber of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Mod
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod \to C^{op}
                  over
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \in C^{op}
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                        %mi Mod
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R Mod
                  of
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi R
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %li
                %p
                  for
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mi 𝒩
                          %mo :
                          %mi 𝒩
                          %mo →
                          %mi R
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi R
                          %mi Mod
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p_{\mathcal{N}} : \mathcal{N} \to R) \in R Mod
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
                  on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                  with coefficients in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒩
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi δ
                        %mo :
                        %mi R
                        %mo →
                        %mi 𝒩
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta : R \to \mathcal{N}
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mi 𝒩
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_{\mathcal{N}}
              %li
                %p
                  The assignment of
                  %strong modules of Kähler differentials
                  or
                  %strong cotangent complexes
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Ω
                          %mi K
                        %mo :
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                        %mo →
                        %mi Mod
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\Omega_K : C^{op} \to Mod
                %p
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} tangent (∞,1)-category
                  projection
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi C
                                %mi op
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_{C^{op}}
                %p
                  Its value
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Ω
                          %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_R(R)
                  on an object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \in C^{op}
                  is the module of Kähler differentials on
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Spec
                          %mi R
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec R \in C
          %h2#specific_definitions Specific definitions
          %p
            We spell out very concretely definitions of Kähler differentials for special concrete choices of base category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            as special cases of the above general story. We start with the familiar cases and then work our way up to more general or richer cases.
          %h3#OrdinaryRings Over ordinary rings
          %p
            In terms of the above discussion, we now take
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi CRing
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = CRing^{op}
            to be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
            of the category of ordinary (commutative unital)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            in question is equipped with a ring homomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \to R
            from a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
          %p
            Suppose
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"} commutative algebra
            over a field
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p
            The simplest construction, maybe, is as follows. The module of
            %strong Kähler differentials
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi K
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1_K(A)
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is generated by symbols
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d a
            for all
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\in A
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mi c
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d c = 0
                when
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
                is a ‘constant’, that is, an element of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                regarded as an element of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi b
                      %mo +
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(a b)=(d a)b+a(d b)
                \.
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo +
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi d
                      %mi a
                      %mo +
                      %mi d
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(a+b)=d a+d b
                \.
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi b
                      %mo =
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (d a)b = b(d a)
                \.
          %p In particular there are only finite sums in the module of Kähler differentials.
          %p
            Another more sophisticated construction of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi K
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1_K(A)
            is given below. But turning to the universal property, note that we can define
            %strong derivations
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to any
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            = succeed "-linear" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X : A \to M
            satisfying the product rule:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi b
                  %mo +
                  %mi a
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X(a b) = X(a) b + a X(b)
          %p
            Then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi K
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1_K(A)
            may be defined as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi K
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d : A \to \Omega^1_K(A),
          %p
            and if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X:A\to M
            is any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to some
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi K
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_X:\Omega_K^1(A)\to M
          %p such that the following diagram commutes:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mi M
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo ↘
                            %mi d
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                          %msub
                            %mi μ
                            %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mi K
                            %mn 1
                          %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  A&amp;\overset{X}\to     &amp; M\\
                  \&amp; \underset{d}\searr&amp;\uparrow \mu_X\\
                  \&amp;                   &amp; \Omega_K^1{A}
                  }
          %p
            We say that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %strong factors through
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
          %h4#relative_version Relative version
          %p
            We can replace the commutative algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            more generally by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+unital+rings"} commutative unital rings
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi R
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:R\to S
            %strong module of Kähler differentials
            is the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi K
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1_K(S/R)
            corepresenting the functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Der
                    %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                  %mo :
                  %mi M
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi Der
                    %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Der_R(S,f_*(-)) : S Mod\to Set : M\mapsto Der_R(S,f_* M)
          %p
            that assigns to every
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivations"} derivations
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            with values in the (bi)module
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_* M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*:S Mod\to R Mod
            is the restriction of scalars.
          %p
            In other words,
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Der
                      %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi K
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Der_R(S,f_*M)\cong Hom_S(\Omega^1_K(S/R),M)
            = succeed "-derivation" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\colon S \to M
            there is a unique morphism (of
            = succeed "-modules)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi K
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu\colon \Omega^1_K(S/R) \to M
            making the following diagram commute:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi S
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mi M
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo ↘
                            %mi d
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                          %mi μ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mi K
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi S
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi R
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  S&amp;\overset{X}\to     &amp; M\\
                  \&amp; \underset{d}\searr&amp;\uparrow \mu\\
                  \&amp;                   &amp; \Omega^1_K(S/R)
                  }
          %p This framework also gives another construction of the module of Kähler differentials, instead of the generators and relations definition given above.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            be the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/augmentation+ideal"} augmentation ideal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
            of the multiplication map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi Ker
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi R
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I := Ker(m:S\otimes_R S\to S)
          %p
            Then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi K
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi R
                  %mo =
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msup
                    %mi I
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1_K_{S/R}= I/I^2
            and there is a canonical induced map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi R
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d: S\to \Omega^1_{S/R}
            given by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mi s
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi s
                    %mo −
                    %mi s
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d s = [1\otimes s - s\otimes 1]
          %h4#higher_degree_khler_forms Higher degree Kähler forms
          %p
            Furthermore, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is in characteristic zero, one may introduce
            %strong
              Kähler
              = succeed "-forms" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            , which are elements of the
            = succeed "-th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exterior+power"} exterior power
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi K
                      %mi p
                    %msub
                      %mo
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi R
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi R
                      %mi p
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi K
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^p_K_{S/R}:=\Lambda_R^p \Omega^1_K_{S/R}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            of Kähler differentials readily generalizes as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            of Kähler differentials for a separated morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:X\to Y
            of (commutative)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schemes"} schemes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            along the embedding of the ideal sheaf of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal+subobject"} diagonal subscheme
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Y
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\hookrightarrow X\times_Y X
          %p
            Compare the role of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+differential+envelope"} universal differential envelope
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Amitsur+complex"} Amitsur complex
            for analogous constructions in the noncommutative case. The appropriate extension of the module of relative Kähler differentials to the derived setting is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotangent+complex"} cotangent complex
            of Grothendieck–Illusie.
          %h4#relation_to_hochschild_homology Relation to Hochschild homology
          %p
            The module of Kähler differentials on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is isomorphic to the first
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hochschild+homology"} Hochschild homology
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi K
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi HH
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega_K^1(R) \simeq HH_1(R,R)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Under mild conditions the analogous statement is true for higher Kähler differentials and higher Hochschild homology: this is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hochschild-Kostant-Rosenberg+theorem"} Hochschild-Kostant-Rosenberg theorem
          %h3#SmoothOrPlain Over smooth rings regarded as ordinary rings
          %blockquote
            %p
              See also at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+C%5E%E2%88%9E-differentials+of+smooth+functions+are+differential+1-forms"} Kähler C^∞-differentials of smooth functions are differential 1-forms
          %p
            We have seen that we define Kähler differentials
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi K
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1_K(A)
            for any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"} commutative algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p The following special case deserves special attention:
          %p
            The algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = C^\infty(X)
            of smooth functions on some smooth space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            or a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+space"} generalized smooth space
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            – in analogy to the case when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            consists of the algebraic functions on an affine
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+variety"} algebraic variety
            in which case Kähler differentials are often taken as a
            %em definition
            of 1-forms.
          %h4#the_problem_and_its_solution The problem and its solution
          %p
            However, when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = C^\infty(X)
            consists of smooth functions on a manifold, the
            %em ring theoretic
            Kähler differentials do
            %em not
            agree with the ordinary smooth
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} 1-form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is, for instance, the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
          %p But there is a solution to this, and an explanation for why something goes wrong:
          %p
            Smooth spaces such as
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            %em not
            modeled on the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CRing"} CRing
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mrow
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}^{op}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/varieties"} varieties
            are. Instead, they are modeled on the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                  %mi 𝕃
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = \mathbb{L}
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+loci"} smooth loci
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %msup
                    %mi Ring
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} = C^\infty Ring^{op}
            the opposite of the category of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+algebra"} C-infinity rings
          %p
            In particular, the algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = C^\infty(X)
            of smooth functions on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            carries naturally the structure of such a
            = succeed "-ring." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty
          %p
            If we do regard
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)
            as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+algebra"} C-infinity ring
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h4#DetailedComparison Detailed comparison
          %p
            We discuss how Kähler differential forms relate to the ordinary notion of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
          %p
            Since there are only finite sums in the module of Kähler differentials, the usual
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi f
                  %mo =
                  %mi f
                  %mo ′
                  %mi d
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d f=f' d t
            works only if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is a finite polynomial in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(\mathbb{R})
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+map"}> smooth maps
            ) or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}[\![t]\!]
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+series"}> power series
            ). For example, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = t^n
            then
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi d
                          %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi d
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi t
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %msup
                            %mi t
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mi d
                          %mi t
                          %mo +
                          %mi t
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi d
                          %msup
                            %mi t
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mn 2
                          %msup
                            %mi t
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mi d
                          %mi t
                          %mo +
                          %msup
                            %mi t
                            %mn 2
                          %mi d
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi t
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi r
                          %msup
                            %mi t
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mi d
                          %mi t
                          %mo +
                          %msup
                            %mi t
                            %mi r
                          %mi d
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi t
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mi r
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi n
                          %msup
                            %mi t
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mi d
                          %mi t
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi f
                          %mo ′
                          %mi d
                          %mi t
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  d f &amp;=
                  d(t^n)  \\
                  \&amp;= t^{n-1} d t  + t(d t^{n-1}) \\
                  \&amp;= 2 t^{n-1} d t + t^2 d(t^{n-2}) \\
                  \&amp;= r t^{n-1} d t + t^r d(t^{n-r}) \\
                  \&amp;= n t^{n-1} d t \\
                  \&amp;= f' d t \,.
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p However, we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mi t
                  %mo ≠
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mi t
                  %mi d
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d e^t \ne e^t d t
          %p
            as Kähler differentials. Intuitively, the reason is that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            cannot pass through the infinite sum
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mi t
                  %mo =
                  %mi d
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %mn ∞
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi t
                          %mi n
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo !
                    %mo )
                  %mo ≠
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %mn ∞
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi t
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo !
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mi t
                  %mi d
                  %mi t
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d e^t = d\left(\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{t^n}{n!}\right) \ne \sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{d(t^n)}{n!} = e^t d t \,.
          %p
            However, the only proof we know that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mi t
                  %mo ≠
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mi t
                  %mi d
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d e^t \ne e^t d t
            is quite tricky: in fact it uses the
            = succeed "!" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
          %ul
            %li#Speyer09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Speyer"}> David Speyer
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Kähler differentials and ordinary differentials
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/a/9723/381"} MO:a/9723
          %p It would be desirable to either find a proof that avoids the Axiom of Choice, or show that axioms beyond ZF are necessary for this result.
          %p
            To avoid this annoying property of Kähler differentials we can proceed as follows. Given a commutative algebra
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Der
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Der(A)
            be the
            = succeed "-bimodule" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            Define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1(A)
            to be the dual of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Der
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Der(A)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi Der
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1(A) = Der(A)^*
          %p
            in other words, the set of
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo :
                    %mi Der
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega : Der(A) \to A
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d : A \to \Omega^1(A)
          %p given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d f (X) = X(f)
          %p
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Der
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in Der(A)
          %p
            Now, suppose
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A=C^\infty(M)
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is any smooth manifold. Then elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1(A)
            can be identified with ordinary smooth 1-forms on
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
          %p
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hadamard+lemma"} Hadamard lemma
            it follows that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Der
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Der(C^\infty(M)) = \Gamma(T M)
            is precisely the
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+field"} vector field
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} 1-forms
            are the
            = succeed "-linear" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)
          %p
            And in this case, one can show that any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X: A \to M
            factors through
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1(A)
            when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is free, and in particular if
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M=A
          %p
            We can expand on this remark as follows. Quite generally, for any commutative algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            over a field
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Der
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi K
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Der(A) \cong \Omega^1_K(A)^*
          %p
            by the universal property of Kähler differentials, which identifies derivations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to A
            with
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi K
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1_K(A) \to A
          %p Using the definition
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi Der
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1(A) = Der(A)^*
          %p
            (of ordinary smooth 1-forms in the case that
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = C^\infty(M)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi K
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1(A) \cong \Omega^1_K(A)^{**}
          %p There is always a homomorphism from a module to its double dual, so we have a morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo :
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi K
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j: \Omega^1_K(A) \to \Omega^1(A)
          %p
            In the case when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = C^\infty(M)
            this map is onto but typically not one-to-one, as witnessed by the fact that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mi t
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mi t
                  %mi d
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d e^t = e^t d t
            in the ordinary 1-forms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1(A)
            but not in the Kähler differentials
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi K
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1_K(A)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is a free
            = succeed "-module," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X: A \to M
            not only factors through
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi K
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1_K(A)
            (as guaranteed by the universal property of Kähler differentials), but also
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1(A)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1(A)
            is torsionless. So
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi K
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1_K(A)
            is the universal differential module for all modules, while
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1(A)
            is the universal differential module for torsionless
            = succeed "-modules." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .query
            %p
              %span.newWikiWord
                Martin Gisser
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Martin+Gisser"} ?
              Couldn’t resist the above uncredentialed drive-by edit…
            %p Is it torsionlessness that ultimately discerns differential geometry from algebraic geometry? (Need to fill in more dots between torsionless modules and “geometric modules” in the sense of Jet Nestruev.)
            %hr/
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric"}> Eric
              \: Does this universal property mean that there is some diagram in some category for which the Kähler differentials can be thought of as a (co)limit?
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              \: Yeah, take the category all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              modules
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              equipped with a derivation
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X : A \to M
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi K
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1_K(A)
            %p
              But this is just a cutesy way to say that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi K
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1_K(A)
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
              of this category.
            %p
              And
              = succeed "," do
                %em this
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi K
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d : A \to \Omega^1_K(A),
            %p
              such that if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X:A\to M
              is also a derivation, then there exists a unique
              = succeed "-module" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi K
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_X:\Omega_K^1(A)\to M
            %p such that the following diagram commutes:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mi M
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ↘
                              %mi d
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                            %msub
                              %mi μ
                              %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mi K
                              %mn 1
                            %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A&amp;\overset{X}\to     &amp; M\\
                    \&amp; \underset{d}\searr&amp;\uparrow \mu_X\\
                    \&amp;                   &amp; \Omega_K^1{A}
                    }
            %p All this is general abstract nonsense, nothing special to this example! Any universal property involving maps out of an object says that object is initial in some category — and that, in turn, is equivalent to saying that object is the colimit of the enormous diagram consisting of all objects of the same kind! There’s a lot less here than meets the eye.
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric"}> Eric
              \: Thank you! That actually makes a little sense to me. As trivial as it may seem, the fact that I was even able to ask this question represents tremendous progress :)
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Herman+Stel"}> Herman Stel
              \: Dear Eric and Prof. Baez. There is a mistake in the explanation by John Baez here. The two latter properties (both being that the derivation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi K
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d : A \to \Omega^1_K(A)
              is initial) are correct. The first one is not, though. If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi K
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1_K(A)
              were the colimit of the huge diagram then for every derivation there would be a morphism from that derivation to the universal derivation, which is not true. Instead, note that an initial object is the vertex of a colimit of the empty diagram in any category (use that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∀
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall x\in X P(x)
              is true if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is empty).
          %h3#CooCase Over smooth rings
          %p
            A
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty
              \-ring
            (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+algebra"} generalized smooth algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
          %p
            If we take a smooth function ring
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo =
                    %mi 𝕃
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %msup
                      %mi Ring
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = \mathbb{L} = C^\infty Ring^{op}
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
          %p
            For the moment, this case is described in detail in the entry on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fermat+theory"} Fermat theory
          %h3#over_general_monoids Over general monoids
          %p
            An ordinary (commutative)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            is precisely a comutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ab
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab
            of abelian
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %a{:href => "#OrdinaryRings"} above
            may therefore be thought of as the case where the category of test objects is taken to be
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi CMon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Ab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C = (CMon(Ab))^{op}
                  \\,.
          %p
            This has an evident generalization: we may replace here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ab
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab
            with
            %em any
            category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            and consider
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi CMon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C = (CMon(K))^{op}
                  \\,.
          %p
            In practice
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is usually required to be an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
          %p
            for any such
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            fixed we follow the
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#AbstractDef"} general definition
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi Ab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi I
                  %mo ,
                  %mi CMon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi CMon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  p : Mod := Ab([I,CMon(K)^{op}]) \to CMon(K)^{op}
          %p
            and define the assignment of
            %strong Kähler differentials
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi K
                  %mo :
                  %mi CMon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi I
                  %mo ,
                  %mi CMon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega_K : CMon(K)^{op} \to Ab([I,CMon(K)^{op}])
          %p
            to be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            of this functor.
          %p
            For this to make good sense, everything here should be regarded as taking place in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} modeled
            by the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+ring"} model structure on simplicial rings
          %p
            Then one finds that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi sCRing
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = sCRing^{op}
            the corresponding notion of module
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            reproduces the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+category"} derived category
            of ordinary ring modules. This is Example 8.6. in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                Stable
                = succeed "-categories" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              \.
          %h4#over_simplicial_rings Over simplicial rings
          %p
            If in the above setup we choose
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo =
                  %mi sAb
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Ab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K = sAb = [\Delta^{op}, Ab]
            the category of abelian
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+group"} simplicial group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Mon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mon(K)
            is the category of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+ring"} simplicial ring
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mon(K)^{op}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
            in place of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi CRing
                    %mrow
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing^{}
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+bundle"} canonical bundle
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotangent+complex"}> cotangent complex
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9-Quillen+homology"} André-Quillen homology
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+Andr%C3%A9-Quillen+homology"} topological André-Quillen homology
          %h2#references References
          %h3#on_smooth_rings_regarded_as_ordinary_rings On smooth rings regarded as ordinary rings
          %p
            For a proof that every derivation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = C^\infty(\mathbb{R})
            comes from a smooth vector field on the real line, and an extensive discussion of Kähler differentials versus ordinary 1-forms, see:
          %ul
            %li
              This Week’s Finds in Mathematical Physics (
              %a{:href => "http://math.ucr.edu/home/baez/week287.html"}> Week 287
              )
          %p
            See also the discussion at the
            = succeed "-Caf\u00E9:" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Blog discussion of Week 287. (
                %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2009/12/this_weeks_finds_in_mathematic_48.html#c030626"}> Summary
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://ocw.mit.edu/NR/rdonlyres/Mathematics/18-726Spring-2009/8C4F62C5-7AE2-482B-9643-890EE76499F5/0/MIT18_726s09_lec13_differentials.pdf"}> The module of Kähler differentials
                , MIT OpenCourseWare: 18.726 Algebraic Geometry, Spring 2009.
          %h3#on_the_fully_general_case On the fully general case
          %p
            A detailed discussion of Kähler differentials and their generalization from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+algebra"} higher algebra
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deformation+Theory"} Deformation Theory
          %h3#for_a_categorical_approach For a categorical approach,
          %p introducing a setting in which Kahler differentials live quite naturally (but not yet in as much generality as possibly one might hope), see
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/R.+Blute"}> R. Blute
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.R.B.+Cockett"} J.R.B. Cockett
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T.+Porter"} T. Porter
              = succeed "," do
